       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 800 mg three or four times daily. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day. A single dose is generally capped at 800 mg.\n- **Risk:** This order is twice the maximum daily dose and twice the maximum single dose. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with your rationale. I can then enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it."
